NAME
    pager - present stdin or files through the RumiAI technical pager abstraction

SYNOPSIS
    pager [file ...]

DESCRIPTION
    pager provides the technical paging boundary used by commands that need
    terminal presentation without embedding host-specific pager selection.

    With no file operands, pager reads standard input. This is the conventional
    pager form used by programs that pipe their output to a pager command.

    With one or more file operands, every pathname is resolved through the
    runtime path-resolution facility and must identify a readable regular file.
    Multiple files are presented in operand order.

    pager intentionally provides the common pager role; it does not attempt to
    reproduce every command-line option accepted by less or more.

OUTPUT DESTINATION
    When standard output is not a terminal, pager is non-interactive.

    With no file operands it copies standard input directly to standard output.
    With file operands it concatenates the resolved files to standard output in
    operand order.

    When standard output is a terminal, pager selects the host viewer described
    below. The viewer reads standard input when no file operand is present and
    receives the resolved file operands otherwise.

BACKEND POLICY
    Prefer less whenever it is available on the current host.

    less is an optional host capability rather than a POSIX baseline
    dependency. If it is unavailable, fall back to the POSIX more utility.
    The fallback is deliberately accepted as a less capable paging experience
    rather than failing solely because less is unavailable.

CALLER ENVIRONMENT
    pager does not erase environment intended for the selected viewer.

    In particular, when less is selected, inherited variables such as LESS,
    LESSOPEN and LESSCLOSE remain available to less. This allows callers such as
    Git to retain their normal pager presentation policy while still using
    pager as the pager command.

    pager does not expose a separate user-configurable backend command. Backend
    selection remains owned by pager itself.

OPERANDS
    file
        Existing readable regular file to present. Zero or more file operands
        are accepted.

EXIT STATUS
    0   Success.
    1   Input/file resolution/access or presentation/backend failure.
    2   Invalid invocation.

